The wall-motion tracking step — aorta-mesh-morphing/select_cut.py,
aorta-mesh-morphing/deformation.py and aorta-mesh-morphing/centerline_simp.py —
is the implementation of the deformation-tracking framework first published as:

    R. Valente, A. Mourato, A. Carvalho, J. Xavier, M. Brito, S. Avril,
    A. Tomás, J. Fragata. Patient-Specific In-vivo Dynamic Motion of Ascending
    Thoracic Aortic Aneurysms from Cine CTA. IEEE Transactions on Biomedical
    Engineering (2026). doi:10.1109/TBME.2026.3681119

No code was released with that paper. It is published here for the first time,
with the agreement of its authors, given in August 2026. Two of them, André
Mourato and Alda Carvalho, are authors of this software but not of the article
this repository accompanies.

This product includes code derived from flow4D, used to decode the 4D flow MRI
acquisitions:

